{"tool_name":"ipc","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ipc","home":"http://isoelectric.org","license":"Other","summary":"Web service and standalone program for the estimation of protein and peptide pI using different sets of dissociation constant (pKa) values, including computationally optimized pKa sets. According to the benchmarks, the newly developed pKa sets outperform previous algorithms by at least 14.9 % for proteins and 0.9 % for peptides (on average, 22.1 % and 59.6 %, respectively), which corresponds to an average error of the pI estimation of 0.87 and 0.25 pH units, respectively.","addition_date":"2017-03-17T14:02:52Z","last_update_date":"2021-09-23T09:59:14.239056Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web service"],"version":["1.0"],"collections":["Proteomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:ipc","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"email":"lukasz.kozlowski.lpk@gmail.com","name":"Lukasz Kozlowski","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-8187-1980","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://bioinformatics.netmark.pl"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://isoelectric.org/algorithms.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"}}],"note":"Isoelectric point, molecular weight","operation":[{"term":"Protein property calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0250"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein isoelectric point","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1528"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"IPC","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"lukaskoz","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13062-016-0159-9","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 The Author(s).Background: Accurate estimation of the isoelectric point (pI) based on the amino acid sequence is useful for many analytical biochemistry and proteomics techniques such as 2-D polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis, or capillary isoelectric focusing used in combination with high-throughput mass spectrometry. Additionally, pI estimation can be helpful during protein crystallization trials. Results: Here, I present the Isoelectric Point Calculator (IPC), a web service and a standalone program for the accurate estimation of protein and peptide pI using different sets of dissociation constant (pKa) values, including two new computationally optimized pKa sets. According to the presented benchmarks, the newly developed IPC pKa sets outperform previous algorithms by at least 14.9 % for proteins and 0.9 % for peptides (on average, 22.1 % and 59.6 %, respectively), which corresponds to an average error of the pI estimation equal to 0.87 and 0.25 pH units for proteins and peptides, respectively. Moreover, the prediction of pI using the IPC pKa's leads to fewer outliers, i.e., predictions affected by errors greater than a given threshold. Conclusions: The IPC service is freely available at http://isoelectric.ovh.org Peptide and protein datasets used in the study and the precalculated pI for the PDB and some of the most frequently used proteomes are available for large-scale analysis and future development. Reviewers: This article was reviewed by Frank Eisenhaber and Zolt\u00e1n G\u00e1sp\u00e1ri","authors":[{"name":"Kozlowski L.P."}],"citationCount":163,"date":"2016-10-21T00:00:00Z","journal":"Biology Direct","title":"IPC - Isoelectric Point Calculator"},"pmcid":"PMC5075173","pmid":"27769290","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Biochemistry","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3292"},{"term":"Molecular biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3047"},{"term":"Protein properties","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0123"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"}